pocket-motion-only: `<Svg>` expands a file into `<Path>`s, and only 0042's PATH op draws them; an upstream target would get Views selecting table entries no backend renders, so the import ships with the op or not at all.

0053 — an SVG file as a tree of nodes: `<Svg src="./x.svg" parts={{ id: "…" }} />`
expanded by the build into Views and `<Path>`s, each element's id its
debugName, so a part can be animated, asserted and swept by name. The
design is `patches/0042-vector-paths.design.md`, "SVG import".

What the patch adds, by file:

- `framework/compiler/svg-tree.ts` (new): the document half. An XML reader
  (comments, processing instructions, CDATA and the doctype dropped; an
  entity declaration refused); the presentation cascade — attributes,
  `style=""` over them, the inherited properties and `inherit`; every basic
  shape as SVG 2's equivalent path (a circle from (cx + r, cy) clockwise, a
  rect from (x + rx, y), so a draw-on starts where a browser's does); every
  `transform` (matrix, translate, scale, rotate, skewX, skewY, the rightmost
  applied first), the viewBox and preserveAspectRatio (nine alignments,
  meet, slice, none) FOLDED into the outline, rotations and skews through
  path-data.ts's `cosSinDeg`, never `Math.cos`; each part's box its own
  bounds, half a stroke out, on whole px, with the outline written relative
  to it, so a part's transform origin is its own centre; paint as class
  tokens — `fill-[#rrggbbaa]` with fill-opacity folded into the alpha, the
  stroke's width scaled by the map, join, cap, miter limit, fill rule,
  `opacity-N`. A stroke under a map that is not a uniform scale and rotation
  is refused: folded into px it would be one width where SVG draws it wider
  along one axis. A `<g>` with an id is a View holding its children in its
  own box; one with neither id nor opacity adds no node. Refused, naming the
  element and its line: gradients, patterns, clip paths, masks, filters,
  `<use>`, `<symbol>`, `<style>`, text, images, nested `<svg>`, markers,
  `<switch>`, `<a>`, scripts and SMIL — inside `<defs>` too; a `url()` paint,
  a dash array, clip-path/mask/filter/marker/vector-effect/paint-order/blend
  properties; a duplicate id. `svgSites` finds the `<Svg src>` elements of a
  module by parsing it, for this repository's lint.
- `framework/compiler/jsx-plugin.ts`: a Babel plugin ahead of the collector
  replaces each JSX element named by a binding imported as `Svg` from the
  framework's components with the expansion — a View with the author's
  class, debugName and other attributes; a canvas View named `svg:<src>` at
  the picture's size, `overflow-hidden` unless the root says
  overflow="visible"; the parts — and adds the View and Path specifiers to
  the import. A `parts` entry is joined to its part's own tokens HERE, as one
  string literal carrying the entry's location (a ternary of them for a
  ternary), so the collector reads it as the whole value of a `class=`
  attribute: 0011's, 0012's and 0041's refusals reach the author's tokens,
  and 0041's is located at the entry. A key naming no id is refused at the
  key, listing the file's ids in document order. `CacheEntry.svgDeps` holds
  every file an expansion read by sha256, and a cached transform is a miss
  when one has changed: the module's own text did not.
- `tools/build.ts`: an `SvgExpandError` is printed as
  `error: file:line:column: <Svg>: …` and the build exits 1.
- `framework/src/primitives.ts`, `components.ts`: `Svg` and `SvgProps`. The
  function runs only when the build did not see the element, and throws
  saying so.

Red cases, run by `baselines/svg-import/redcheck.ts`, each an edit to one or
two `+` lines of this patch (the harness rebuilds the vendored tree from the
edited patch and restores it) — or, for the last four, to this repository's
own file — each turning the named test red:
- a circle swept counter-clockwise -> tests/svg-import.test.ts -t a circle starts at
- a transform list composed leftmost-first -> -t a transform list applies its rightmost function first
- rotate() through Math.cos and Math.sin -> -t a quarter turn is exact
- meet and slice swapped -> -t preserveAspectRatio
- a stroke under a non-uniform map accepted -> -t non-uniform map is refused
- a gradient not refused by name -> -t refused: <defs><linearGradient
- ids listed in the order the walk finished them -> -t an unnamed group is folded
- an editor's unit on the root's size refused without saying what to give -> -t an editor's unit on the root's size
- an id inside <defs> not recorded -> -t an id inside <defs> is known
- the expander not among transformFile's plugins -> -t every shape is an outline the collector bakes
- the added import names forgotten between elements -> -t two <Svg> elements in one module
- a parts key naming no id accepted -> -t a parts key naming no id
- a parts entry joined as a `+` expression, not a literal -> -t a token in a parts value that does not parse
- a parts entry dropped from the join -> -t sidecar's assertions hold
- a cached transform kept when its file changed -> -t a cached transform is dropped
- the canvas not named svg:<src> -> -t every shape is an outline the collector bakes
- the catalogue's svg probe expecting the wrong refusal (src/catalog/surface.ts) -> tests/catalog.test.ts -t G10
- lint does not check the file exists (src/lint/svg-trees.ts) -> -t a missing file is svg.missingFile
- the image lint reads an <Svg>'s src as a picture name (src/lint/images.ts) -> -t a missing file is svg.missingFile
- layout reads one picture's parts as collisions (src/render/findings.ts) -> -t two parts in one svg

The fixture is `compositions/svg-import`, in both ledgers: a line-art
lighthouse whose parts are drawn on one after another, a lamp that pops
about its own centre and a beam that sweeps about the lamp, its sidecar
asserting the order by id.

`git apply` skips everything above the first `diff --git`.

